From: Balamurugan Mahalingam <bmahalin@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 30 May 2025 22:20:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: fix PPE2TCL descriptor stride

The QCN9274 PPE2TCL ring is shared with the IPQ9574 EDMA v2 RXDESC
primary ring.  EDMA advances that ring in 32-byte descriptors, matching
the downstream QSDK definition of tcl_entrance_from_ppe_ring as eight
dwords.

The current ath12k definition only contains the first two dwords.  It
therefore allocates and programs the SRNG with an 8-byte entry stride,
while EDMA writes with a 32-byte stride.  Besides making the producer and
consumer indices refer to different locations, this lets EDMA write past
the allocated PPE2TCL ring and prevents PPE-to-WLAN traffic from reaching
TCL.

Restore the complete QSDK descriptor layout.  The trailing fields are
written by EDMA and consumed by TCL; ath12k does not need to interpret
them in software.

Based-on: 4590caf67ab7de99e7a1ea2bc70d2429b5f855e1
Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/system/feeds/wlan-open/-/blob/1ee3a4ab7c59ceaff347c4668fc6c7604a04c323/patches/ath12k/0337-01-QSDK-DP-wifi-Add-support-for-PPE-DS-Direct-switch-fe.patch
